-- Catalog expansion round 5 (2026-09-21): bibliographic ingestion only,
-- deliberately NOT tagged yet (tagging is a separate future step) -- same
-- pattern as prior expansion rounds (20260830040000, 20260831020000,
-- 20260902040000, 20260912000000). Generated by scripts/ingest-catalog-round5.js
-- against hosted directly (this environment has no local Supabase stack --
-- confirmed 2026-09-21, only DATABASE_URL/HARDCOVER_API_TOKEN exist in .env).
--
-- UNLIKE round 4 (which bumped the raw pull count and inserted every new
-- hardcover_id unconditionally, then found ~1/3 of the 378 new books were
-- non-SFF leakage on a later audit -- see docs/project-log.md's 2026-09-21
-- archival entry), this round applies a real pre-insertion quality filter,
-- using two structured signals discovered via GraphQL introspection against
-- Hardcover's books type (not previously used by any ingestion script here):
--   1. book_category_id (Hardcover's own format classification) -- excludes
--      Graphic Novel/Fan Fiction/Research Paper/Poetry (ids 4/5/6/7).
--   2. books.cached_tags.Genre -- real per-tag community vote counts (NOT
--      just the loose genres:=[X] search filter, and NOT just the search
--      index's genre list position, which turned out to have real small-
--      sample false positives -- see docs/project-log.md's round-5 entry
--      for the full calibration writeup). A candidate is kept only if a
--      Fantasy/Science-Fiction-pattern tag holds the single highest raw
--      vote count among all Genre tags, with a minimum-sample floor.
-- A further 144-book bucket had too few community genre tags for that
-- vote-count rule to apply at all (new/niche titles); these were screened
-- individually against title/author/synopsis using real literary knowledge
-- per this round's task instructions, rather than either blanket-accepted
-- or blanket-discarded (108 kept, 36 rejected) -- see docs/project-log.md
-- for the method and worked rejection examples from that manual screen
-- (Dostoevsky's 'Devils', Murakami's 'Sputnik Sweetheart', the GRRM
-- 'World of Ice and Fire' companion book, etc.) and from the automated
-- vote-count rule above it (Ken Follett's WWI novel 'Fall of Giants',
-- Kafka's 'The Castle', Stephen Fry's nonfiction-tagged 'Heroes', etc.).
--
-- COVER IMAGES: cover_url below is Hardcover's own asset URL, stored
-- directly -- NOT self-hosted via scripts/lib/self-host-cover.js, because
-- this environment has no supabase link / Storage access (no service-role
-- key, no linked project). This is a deliberate, documented deviation from
-- the 2026-09-18 self-hosting convention (see CLAUDE.md's ingestion
-- conventions) -- these 226 covers still need to go through
-- the self-hosting backfill pipeline from a machine that HAS Supabase
-- Storage access (CLDO's or the repo owner's own machine).
--
-- 85 new series (hardcover-sourced, deduped by Hardcover's
-- own series id per the existing ingestion script pattern).

-- ===== 85 new series (hardcover-sourced) =====
